From 15478cf87b4e23698947bd0253bcd4c335ace787 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 06:40:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rpi3: iOS 10 IOSurface ABI: 0x3c8-byte records, binary
 properties, selector 13

iOS 10's IOSurface client asks for a 0x3c8-byte surface record (same
leading fields as iOS 7's 0x548), sends creation properties in the
binary serialization (0xd3) this kernel could not read, and queries
capabilities with selector 13 (iOS 7: 16). Also log IOSurface and
framebuffer notification-port traffic on serial.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0123xbco8JF8tibbBMLmXceV
